1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,776
September, nineteen seventy-three.

2
00:00:01,836 --> 00:00:04,115
Two engineers at Ford finish an eight-page report

3
00:00:04,116 --> 00:00:06,441
and send it to the federal government.

4
00:00:06,501 --> 00:00:08,645
On page six there is a table.

5
00:00:08,705 --> 00:00:11,221
It counts deaths, and it prices them.

6
00:00:11,281 --> 00:00:13,580
Four years from now a magazine will reprint

7
00:00:13,581 --> 00:00:14,541
that table,

8
00:00:14,601 --> 00:00:16,680
and the country will decide it knows what Ford

9
00:00:16,681 --> 00:00:17,651
did.

10
00:00:17,711 --> 00:00:22,098
Almost nobody will notice what the table is about.

11
00:00:22,158 --> 00:00:24,277
Two of those eight pages describe a car rolling

12
00:00:24,278 --> 00:00:25,184
over.

13
00:00:25,244 --> 00:00:26,643
One more thing before we start,

14
00:00:26,644 --> 00:00:28,223
because it changes how everything

15
00:00:28,224 --> 00:00:30,035
after it should be heard.

16
00:00:30,095 --> 00:00:31,974
Most of what is known about this case comes

17
00:00:31,975 --> 00:00:33,857
from a single appellate opinion,

18
00:00:33,875 --> 00:00:36,114
and that opinion says of itself that it viewed

19
00:00:36,115 --> 00:00:38,134
the evidence in the light most favourable

20
00:00:38,135 --> 00:00:40,923
to the side that had already won.

21
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:42,988
It is not a neutral account.

22
00:00:43,048 --> 00:00:46,413
It was never trying to be.

23
00:00:46,473 --> 00:00:48,552
In nineteen sixty-eight Ford began designing

24
00:00:48,553 --> 00:00:50,057
a new subcompact.

25
00:00:50,117 --> 00:00:52,636
A vice president named Lee Iacocca conceived

26
00:00:52,637 --> 00:00:55,233
the project and was its moving force.

27
00:00:55,293 --> 00:00:56,492
The objective was a car

28
00:00:56,493 --> 00:00:58,472
at or below two thousand pounds,

29
00:00:58,473 --> 00:01:01,756
to sell for no more than two thousand dollars.

30
00:01:01,816 --> 00:01:03,375
The court that later heard the case put

31
00:01:03,376 --> 00:01:04,935
the next part plainly.

32
00:01:04,995 --> 00:01:07,155
The Pinto was a rush project,

33
00:01:07,215 --> 00:01:09,214
so that styling preceded engineering

34
00:01:09,215 --> 00:01:11,314
and dictated engineering design

35
00:01:11,315 --> 00:01:13,362
to a greater degree than usual.

36
00:01:13,422 --> 00:01:15,521
Among the engineering decisions dictated

37
00:01:15,522 --> 00:01:18,492
by styling was the placement of the fuel tank.

38
00:01:18,552 --> 00:01:20,835
The tank went behind the rear axle.

39
00:01:20,895 --> 00:01:22,015
There was a reason,

40
00:01:22,075 --> 00:01:24,061
and it was not a sinister one.

41
00:01:24,121 --> 00:01:26,320
A law professor who read the trial record put it

42
00:01:26,321 --> 00:01:27,281
this way:

43
00:01:27,341 --> 00:01:30,761
if the fuel tank were located above the axle,

44
00:01:30,821 --> 00:01:33,742
the Pinto would have been left
with a very small trunk.

45
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:36,132
That location was not unusual.

46
00:01:36,192 --> 00:01:39,497
It was a commonplace at the time in American cars.

47
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:42,444
What was unusual was what was left behind it.

48
00:01:42,504 --> 00:01:44,203
Between the back of the tank and the rear

49
00:01:44,204 --> 00:01:46,463
of the car there were nine or ten inches

50
00:01:46,464 --> 00:01:49,199
of what engineers call crush space.

51
00:01:49,259 --> 00:01:51,357
The opinion says nine or ten.

52
00:01:51,417 --> 00:01:53,375
Schwartz says nine.

53
00:01:53,435 --> 00:01:54,474
Either way it is less

54
00:01:54,475 --> 00:01:56,514
than any other American automobile,

55
00:01:56,515 --> 00:02:00,037
and less than any Ford subcompact built overseas.

56
00:02:00,097 --> 00:02:01,756
The bumper, in Schwartz's words,

57
00:02:01,757 --> 00:02:03,634
was essentially ornamental.

58
00:02:03,694 --> 00:02:05,333
And here is the kind of sentence

59
00:02:05,334 --> 00:02:07,231
this film keeps having to say.

60
00:02:07,291 --> 00:02:09,871
At the criminal trial eight years later

61
00:02:09,931 --> 00:02:12,230
a witness called by the prosecution was asked

62
00:02:12,231 --> 00:02:13,070
about that bumper,

63
00:02:13,071 --> 00:02:15,350
and said it was about the same as the ones

64
00:02:15,351 --> 00:02:18,259
on the Gremlin, the Vega and the Dodge Colt.

65
00:02:18,319 --> 00:02:20,649
I would say they were all bad.

66
00:02:20,709 --> 00:02:22,528
Ford crash-tested the car.

67
00:02:22,588 --> 00:02:25,067
The tests were run against a fuel-system standard

68
00:02:25,068 --> 00:02:26,987
the federal government had proposed

69
00:02:26,988 --> 00:02:28,633
but not yet imposed.

70
00:02:28,693 --> 00:02:29,892
The results are in the record,

71
00:02:29,893 --> 00:02:31,952
and they are not ambiguous.

72
00:02:32,012 --> 00:02:33,291
The crash tests revealed

73
00:02:33,292 --> 00:02:34,871
that the Pinto's fuel system

74
00:02:34,872 --> 00:02:36,631
as designed could not meet

75
00:02:36,632 --> 00:02:39,138
the twenty-mile-per-hour proposed standard.

76
00:02:39,139 --> 00:02:40,518
At twenty-one miles an hour,

77
00:02:40,519 --> 00:02:42,218
prototypes had the tank driven forward

78
00:02:42,219 --> 00:02:43,466
and punctured.

79
00:02:43,526 --> 00:02:45,705
A production car struck at the same speed

80
00:02:45,706 --> 00:02:48,725
into a fixed barrier had the filler neck torn away

81
00:02:48,726 --> 00:02:49,846
from the tank,

82
00:02:49,906 --> 00:02:52,525
and the tank itself punctured by a bolt head

83
00:02:52,526 --> 00:02:54,354
on the differential housing.

84
00:02:54,414 --> 00:02:55,490
Bolts.

85
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:56,905
On the housing.

86
00:02:56,965 --> 00:02:58,459
Facing the tank.

87
00:02:58,519 --> 00:03:00,278
The federal regulator says the same thing

88
00:03:00,279 --> 00:03:01,638
in its own file.

89
00:03:01,698 --> 00:03:03,097
Its investigation report

90
00:03:03,098 --> 00:03:05,357
of nineteen seventy-eight records

91
00:03:05,358 --> 00:03:07,097
that the Pinto performed badly

92
00:03:07,098 --> 00:03:09,057
in these initial crash tests,

93
00:03:09,058 --> 00:03:11,877
and that Ford responded by somewhat modifying

94
00:03:11,878 --> 00:03:15,406
the Pinto's rear design before production began.

95
00:03:15,466 --> 00:03:18,864
The fixes had prices, and the opinion lists them.

96
00:03:18,924 --> 00:03:22,275
A smooth differential housing, two dollars ten.

97
00:03:22,335 --> 00:03:24,754
A shock-absorbent flak suit around the tank,

98
00:03:24,755 --> 00:03:25,919
four dollars.

99
00:03:25,979 --> 00:03:26,818
A nylon bladder,

100
00:03:26,819 --> 00:03:29,343
between five twenty-five and eight dollars.

101
00:03:29,344 --> 00:03:31,484
Eight more inches of crush space,

102
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:33,021
six dollars forty.

103
00:03:33,081 --> 00:03:35,086
And one combined figure.

104
00:03:35,146 --> 00:03:38,497
Another number is going to try to take its place.

105
00:03:38,557 --> 00:03:39,596
Equipping the car

106
00:03:39,597 --> 00:03:43,237
with a reinforced rear structure, a smooth axle,

107
00:03:43,297 --> 00:03:46,317
an improved bumper and additional crush space,

108
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:49,157
at a total cost of fifteen dollars

109
00:03:49,217 --> 00:03:49,996
and thirty cents,

110
00:03:49,997 --> 00:03:51,836
would have made the fuel tank safe

111
00:03:51,837 --> 00:03:53,896
in a rear-end collision at thirty-four

112
00:03:53,897 --> 00:03:55,356
to thirty-eight miles an hour,

113
00:03:55,357 --> 00:03:57,791
by a vehicle the size of a Ford Galaxie.

114
00:03:57,851 --> 00:03:59,252
Fifteen thirty.

115
00:03:59,312 --> 00:04:00,667
Hold on to it.

116
00:04:00,727 --> 00:04:02,506
The results of those tests did not stay

117
00:04:02,507 --> 00:04:03,893
with the engineers.

118
00:04:03,953 --> 00:04:06,332
The court found that the Pinto crash test results

119
00:04:06,333 --> 00:04:08,172
had been forwarded up the chain of command

120
00:04:08,173 --> 00:04:09,632
to the ultimate decision-makers,

121
00:04:09,633 --> 00:04:12,452
and were known to the Ford officials who decided

122
00:04:12,453 --> 00:04:14,363
to go forward with production.

123
00:04:14,423 --> 00:04:18,082
In April nineteen seventy-one there was a product

124
00:04:18,083 --> 00:04:19,028
review meeting.

125
00:04:19,088 --> 00:04:20,861
A report was handed round.

126
00:04:20,921 --> 00:04:23,100
The court describes it as a report prepared

127
00:04:23,101 --> 00:04:24,920
by Ford engineers pertaining

128
00:04:24,921 --> 00:04:26,340
to the financial impact

129
00:04:26,341 --> 00:04:27,940
of a proposed federal standard

130
00:04:27,941 --> 00:04:29,700
on fuel system integrity,

131
00:04:29,701 --> 00:04:32,140
and the cost savings which would accrue

132
00:04:32,141 --> 00:04:34,582
from deferring even minimal fixes.

133
00:04:34,642 --> 00:04:37,250
This document is not the famous one.

134
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:39,036
This one was in evidence.

135
00:04:39,096 --> 00:04:41,295
It is quoted in the opinion's own footnotes,

136
00:04:41,296 --> 00:04:44,255
under the heading Fuel System integrity Program

137
00:04:44,256 --> 00:04:48,252
financial review, and it recommends a delay.

138
00:04:48,312 --> 00:04:50,792
Its recommendation, in its own words:

139
00:04:50,852 --> 00:04:52,071
a design cost savings

140
00:04:52,072 --> 00:04:55,391
of ten point nine million dollars,

141
00:04:55,392 --> 00:04:57,931
for nineteen seventy-four and seventy-five,

142
00:04:57,932 --> 00:04:59,431
can be realised by this delay.

143
00:04:59,432 --> 00:05:01,530
Two more lines from the same paper.

144
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:03,769
Currently there are no plans for forward models

145
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:05,777
to repackage the fuel tanks.

146
00:05:05,837 --> 00:05:06,957
And, of the Pinto:

147
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:09,096
smallest car line with most difficulty

148
00:05:09,097 --> 00:05:10,860
in achieving compliance.

149
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:13,519
In October of that year Ford officials decided

150
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,879
against incorporating any of the modifications

151
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,569
into current Pintos.

152
00:05:17,629 --> 00:05:18,548
The company would wait

153
00:05:18,549 --> 00:05:20,368
until the federal regulator clarified

154
00:05:20,369 --> 00:05:21,770
its position.

155
00:05:21,830 --> 00:05:23,209
The regulator clarified it

156
00:05:23,210 --> 00:05:25,089
in nineteen seventy-three.

157
00:05:25,149 --> 00:05:26,748
It issued the fuel-tank standard,

158
00:05:26,749 --> 00:05:29,408
and ruled that the standard would apply only

159
00:05:29,409 --> 00:05:32,030
to nineteen seventy-seven models.

160
00:05:32,090 --> 00:05:35,223
Four model years away.

161
00:05:35,283 --> 00:05:38,463
On the twenty-eighth of May, nineteen seventy-two,

162
00:05:38,523 --> 00:05:41,082
Mrs Lilly Gray set out in her Pinto from Anaheim

163
00:05:41,083 --> 00:05:43,418
for Barstow, to meet her husband.

164
00:05:43,478 --> 00:05:44,797
The car was six months old

165
00:05:44,798 --> 00:05:46,737
and had been driven approximately three thousand

166
00:05:46,738 --> 00:05:47,758
miles.

167
00:05:47,818 --> 00:05:49,897
A thirteen-year-old neighbour was in the passenger

168
00:05:49,898 --> 00:05:50,891
seat.

169
00:05:50,951 --> 00:05:52,538
She changed lanes.

170
00:05:52,598 --> 00:05:54,737
Then the car stalled and coasted to a halt

171
00:05:54,738 --> 00:05:56,566
in the middle lane of the freeway.

172
00:05:56,567 --> 00:05:58,850
The reason was not the fuel tank.

173
00:05:58,910 --> 00:06:00,189
It was later established

174
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:03,469
that the carburettor float had become so saturated

175
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:06,430
with gasoline that it suddenly sank,

176
00:06:06,490 --> 00:06:08,869
opening the float chamber and causing the engine

177
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:10,388
to flood and stall.

178
00:06:10,448 --> 00:06:12,128
A car came up behind her.

179
00:06:12,188 --> 00:06:15,147
How fast it was going is the single most contested

180
00:06:15,148 --> 00:06:16,627
fact in this entire story,

181
00:06:16,628 --> 00:06:19,394
and both answers are in the record.

182
00:06:19,454 --> 00:06:21,784
The jury took the plaintiffs' version.

183
00:06:21,844 --> 00:06:23,483
The Galaxie had been travelling from fifty

184
00:06:23,484 --> 00:06:25,264
to fifty-five miles per hour,

185
00:06:25,324 --> 00:06:27,623
but before the impact had been braked to a speed

186
00:06:27,624 --> 00:06:28,463
of from twenty-eight

187
00:06:28,464 --> 00:06:30,443
to thirty-seven miles per hour.

188
00:06:30,503 --> 00:06:32,974
Ford's position at trial was the opposite.

189
00:06:33,032 --> 00:06:34,831
Schwartz, who read the record, notes

190
00:06:34,832 --> 00:06:36,931
that the appellate opinion does not mention it

191
00:06:36,932 --> 00:06:38,292
at any point:

192
00:06:38,352 --> 00:06:40,531
Ford's basic position was that the approaching car

193
00:06:40,532 --> 00:06:41,871
had not slowed down at all,

194
00:06:41,872 --> 00:06:43,931
and had struck the Gray car at a speed

195
00:06:43,932 --> 00:06:46,043
in excess of fifty miles per hour.

196
00:06:46,103 --> 00:06:49,722
A nineteen seventy-two Ford Pinto hatchback

197
00:06:49,723 --> 00:06:52,942
automobile unexpectedly stalled on a freeway,

198
00:06:52,943 --> 00:06:54,642
erupting into flames when it was rear ended

199
00:06:54,643 --> 00:06:56,990
by a car proceeding in the same direction.

200
00:06:56,991 --> 00:06:58,810
Mrs Gray died a few days later

201
00:06:58,811 --> 00:07:01,150
of congestive heart failure as a result

202
00:07:01,151 --> 00:07:02,386
of the burns.

203
00:07:02,446 --> 00:07:03,940
The boy survived.

204
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,719
He survived only through heroic medical measures,

205
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,099
and he underwent numerous and extensive surgeries

206
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,556
and skin grafts.

207
00:07:10,616 --> 00:07:12,342
And then the court stops.

208
00:07:12,402 --> 00:07:14,001
Because Ford does not contest the amount

209
00:07:14,002 --> 00:07:16,842
of compensatory damages awarded, it wrote,

210
00:07:16,902 --> 00:07:19,141
no purpose would be served by further description

211
00:07:19,142 --> 00:07:21,466
of the injuries suffered by Grimshaw.

212
00:07:21,526 --> 00:07:24,025
That is a court with every reason to describe

213
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:26,596
those injuries declining to describe them.

214
00:07:26,656 --> 00:07:28,196
He was thirteen.

215
00:07:28,256 --> 00:07:29,889
He is a private person.

216
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:32,969
This film stops where the opinion stopped,

217
00:07:33,029 --> 00:07:34,669
and it will not go past it,

218
00:07:34,729 --> 00:07:37,109
and you have now been told why.

219
00:07:37,169 --> 00:07:40,056
Other defendants settled before and during trial.

220
00:07:40,116 --> 00:07:41,595
The case went to verdict only

221
00:07:41,596 --> 00:07:43,375
against Ford Motor Company.

222
00:07:43,435 --> 00:07:45,393
The trial ran six months.

223
00:07:45,453 --> 00:07:47,829
The jury deliberated for eight hours.

224
00:07:47,889 --> 00:07:53,089
It awarded the boy two million eight hundred

225
00:07:53,149 --> 00:07:55,288
and forty-one thousand dollars

226
00:07:55,289 --> 00:07:56,489
in compensatory damages,

227
00:07:56,490 --> 00:07:56,775
and one hundred and twenty-five million dollars

228
00:07:56,776 --> 00:08:01,545
in punitive damages.
It awarded Mrs Gray's family six hundred

229
00:08:01,605 --> 00:08:02,791
and fifty-nine thousand, six hundred and eighty.

230
00:08:02,792 --> 00:08:03,832
By stipulation,

231
00:08:03,892 --> 00:08:05,551
sums the plaintiffs had already received

232
00:08:05,552 --> 00:08:07,791
from the other defendants were deducted,

233
00:08:07,792 --> 00:08:08,971
and the judgment was entered

234
00:08:08,972 --> 00:08:14,802
at two million five hundred and sixteen thousand,
and five hundred

235
00:08:14,803 --> 00:08:15,537
and fifty-nine thousand six hundred and eighty.

236
00:08:15,538 --> 00:08:17,538
Then Ford moved for a new trial,

237
00:08:17,598 --> 00:08:21,258
and the judge did the thing that is missing
from almost every retelling.

238
00:08:21,318 --> 00:08:23,217
He granted the motion unless the boy gave

239
00:08:23,218 --> 00:08:24,437
the money back.

240
00:08:24,497 --> 00:08:26,737
On Ford's motion for a new trial,

241
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:29,516
Grimshaw was required to remit all but three

242
00:08:29,517 --> 00:08:32,876
and a half million dollars of the punitive award,

243
00:08:32,877 --> 00:08:34,688
as a condition of denial of the motion.

244
00:08:34,689 --> 00:08:36,108
One hundred and twenty-five million,

245
00:08:36,109 --> 00:08:37,901
down to three and a half.

246
00:08:37,961 --> 00:08:40,987
A reduction of ninety-seven point two per cent.

247
00:08:41,047 --> 00:08:43,126
The judge's stated reasons are worth hearing,

248
00:08:43,127 --> 00:08:46,210
because they are not what you would expect.

249
00:08:46,270 --> 00:08:46,749
He noted

250
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:50,530
that Ford's net worth was seven point seven

251
00:08:50,590 --> 00:08:51,349
billion dollars,

252
00:08:51,350 --> 00:08:53,469
and that its profits during the last quarter

253
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:56,469
of the year in the financial statement introduced

254
00:08:56,470 --> 00:08:58,137
into evidence were more than twice

255
00:08:58,138 --> 00:09:00,890
the punitive award.
On that basis the award was not disproportionate

256
00:09:00,891 --> 00:09:02,170
to Ford's net assets,

257
00:09:02,171 --> 00:09:05,525
or to its profit generating capacity.

258
00:09:05,585 --> 00:09:07,172
He reduced it anyway.

259
00:09:07,232 --> 00:09:08,891
His stated reason was proportion

260
00:09:08,892 --> 00:09:10,412
of a different kind:

261
00:09:10,472 --> 00:09:12,931
the amount
of the punitive award was forty-four times

262
00:09:12,932 --> 00:09:14,810
the compensatory award.

263
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:18,361
And he added something that ought
to be quoted more often than it is.

264
00:09:18,421 --> 00:09:20,821
He was not suggesting, he said,

265
00:09:20,881 --> 00:09:22,340
that the amount was warranted,

266
00:09:22,341 --> 00:09:25,920
or that the jury did utilise Exhibit one

267
00:09:25,921 --> 00:09:28,460
twenty-five, or any other exhibits,

268
00:09:28,461 --> 00:09:29,960
and if they did,

269
00:09:29,961 --> 00:09:31,862
that they were justified in so doing.

270
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:36,017
Nobody knows how that jury reached one hundred
and twenty-five million dollars.

271
00:09:36,018 --> 00:09:37,797
The judge who watched the whole trial refused

272
00:09:37,798 --> 00:09:38,859
to guess.

273
00:09:38,919 --> 00:09:41,018
Mrs Gray's family received nothing punitive

274
00:09:41,019 --> 00:09:42,085
at all.

275
00:09:42,145 --> 00:09:44,885
Under California law as it then stood,

276
00:09:44,945 --> 00:09:46,984
punitive damages were not recoverable

277
00:09:46,985 --> 00:09:48,504
in a wrongful death action,

278
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:51,162
and the motion to add them was denied.

279
00:09:51,222 --> 00:09:54,202
The woman who died recovered nothing punitive.

280
00:09:54,262 --> 00:09:55,741
The boy who lived recovered three

281
00:09:55,742 --> 00:09:57,103
and a half million.

282
00:09:57,163 --> 00:09:58,762
The Court of Appeal affirmed all of it

283
00:09:58,763 --> 00:10:01,768
on the twenty-ninth of May, nineteen eighty-one.

284
00:10:01,828 --> 00:10:04,018
A rehearing was denied in June.

285
00:10:04,078 --> 00:10:06,197
The California Supreme Court denied review

286
00:10:06,198 --> 00:10:08,080
on the tenth of September.

287
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:11,830
The appellate court changed no number.

288
00:10:11,890 --> 00:10:14,289
In September nineteen seventy-seven,

289
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:16,349
four years after that eight-page report was posted

290
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:17,550
to Washington,

291
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:19,589
a magazine called Mother Jones published

292
00:10:19,590 --> 00:10:21,511
an article by Mark Dowie.

293
00:10:21,571 --> 00:10:23,808
It was titled Pinto Madness.

294
00:10:23,868 --> 00:10:26,147
The magazine held a press conference in Washington

295
00:10:26,148 --> 00:10:27,359
to launch it.

296
00:10:27,419 --> 00:10:29,981
Dowie was accompanied by Ralph Nader.

297
00:10:30,041 --> 00:10:32,371
The article makes a number of claims.

298
00:10:32,431 --> 00:10:35,086
One of them became the thing everybody knows.

299
00:10:35,146 --> 00:10:37,726
By conservative estimates, Dowie wrote,

300
00:10:37,786 --> 00:10:41,225
Pinto crashes have caused five hundred burn deaths

301
00:10:41,226 --> 00:10:41,645
to people

302
00:10:41,646 --> 00:10:43,765
who would not have been seriously injured

303
00:10:43,766 --> 00:10:46,160
if the car had not burst into flames.

304
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,748
The figure could be as high as nine hundred.

305
00:10:48,749 --> 00:10:51,543
The article gives no source for either number.

306
00:10:51,603 --> 00:10:54,258
Not a footnote, not an agency, not a study.

307
00:10:54,318 --> 00:10:55,797
Two figures, in one sentence,

308
00:10:55,798 --> 00:10:58,691
and nothing behind them in the text.

309
00:10:58,751 --> 00:10:59,970
Then the sentence that became

310
00:10:59,971 --> 00:11:01,870
the whole popular story.

311
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:04,089
Ford waited eight years, Dowie wrote,

312
00:11:04,090 --> 00:11:06,630
because its internal cost-benefit analysis,

313
00:11:06,690 --> 00:11:09,430
which places a dollar value on human life,

314
00:11:09,490 --> 00:11:10,909
said it was not profitable to make

315
00:11:10,910 --> 00:11:12,340
the changes sooner.

316
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:15,194
And the one that misdescribes the document.

317
00:11:15,254 --> 00:11:17,333
This cost-benefit analysis argued

318
00:11:17,334 --> 00:11:18,533
that Ford should not make

319
00:11:18,534 --> 00:11:20,293
an eleven-dollar-per-car improvement

320
00:11:20,294 --> 00:11:22,753
that would prevent one hundred

321
00:11:22,754 --> 00:11:24,098
and eighty fiery deaths a year.

322
00:11:24,099 --> 00:11:26,011
Hold that eleven dollars too.

323
00:11:26,071 --> 00:11:27,565
It comes back.

324
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:30,244
What the article did next is almost never told,

325
00:11:30,245 --> 00:11:30,884
and it produced

326
00:11:30,885 --> 00:11:33,809
the only reliable numbers anybody has.

327
00:11:33,869 --> 00:11:35,701
It moved the federal government.

328
00:11:35,702 --> 00:11:38,021
The regulator's own investigation report opens

329
00:11:38,022 --> 00:11:39,286
on this point.

330
00:11:39,346 --> 00:11:41,565
Following public release of the article,

331
00:11:41,566 --> 00:11:43,725
Pinto Madness, the agency initiated,

332
00:11:43,726 --> 00:11:46,785
on the eleventh of August nineteen seventy-seven,

333
00:11:46,786 --> 00:11:48,485
a preliminary evaluation

334
00:11:48,486 --> 00:11:50,465
of the alleged safety defect,

335
00:11:50,466 --> 00:11:52,485
and on the thirteenth of September,

336
00:11:52,486 --> 00:11:55,004
a formal defect investigation case.

337
00:11:55,064 --> 00:11:56,483
Then it lists what it did,

338
00:11:56,484 --> 00:11:58,369
and the list is worth reading.

339
00:11:58,429 --> 00:12:00,928
The author of the magazine article, Mark Dowie,

340
00:12:00,929 --> 00:12:02,808
was asked to make available to the agency

341
00:12:02,809 --> 00:12:05,148
the documentation and evidence upon

342
00:12:05,149 --> 00:12:07,075
which his article was based.

343
00:12:07,135 --> 00:12:09,429
Congressional inquiries were processed.

344
00:12:09,432 --> 00:12:12,192
The Fatal Accident Reporting System was searched.

345
00:12:12,193 --> 00:12:14,272
Ford was requested to provide technical

346
00:12:14,273 --> 00:12:15,777
and legal data.

347
00:12:15,837 --> 00:12:16,816
And a test program

348
00:12:16,817 --> 00:12:19,076
of staged vehicle-to-vehicle rear-end collisions

349
00:12:19,077 --> 00:12:19,776
was developed,

350
00:12:19,777 --> 00:12:21,996
and a contract awarded for the performance

351
00:12:21,997 --> 00:12:23,322
of these tests.

352
00:12:23,382 --> 00:12:25,081
Over nine hundred inquiries came

353
00:12:25,082 --> 00:12:26,269
in from the public.

354
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:28,468
Of all of them, one letter reported a fire

355
00:12:28,469 --> 00:12:30,763
the agency had not already heard about.

356
00:12:30,809 --> 00:12:33,048
A parked Pinto, struck from behind

357
00:12:33,049 --> 00:12:36,008
by a nineteen sixty-nine Pontiac Firebird,

358
00:12:36,009 --> 00:12:37,504
in a residential area.

359
00:12:37,564 --> 00:12:38,543
No bodily injuries

360
00:12:38,544 --> 00:12:40,683
and no fatalities were sustained.

361
00:12:40,743 --> 00:12:43,584
Ford was asked for its own count, and gave it.

362
00:12:43,644 --> 00:12:45,303
Thirty-five rear-impact fuel-leakage

363
00:12:45,304 --> 00:12:46,717
or fire cases.

364
00:12:46,777 --> 00:12:49,478
Twenty-nine lawsuits and liability claims.

365
00:12:49,538 --> 00:12:51,678
Twenty-six fatalities reported,

366
00:12:51,738 --> 00:12:54,608
of which twenty-five were Pinto occupants.

367
00:12:54,668 --> 00:12:56,147
And a breakdown of the claims

368
00:12:56,148 --> 00:12:57,467
that is worth putting beside

369
00:12:57,468 --> 00:12:59,027
the phrase everyone remembers

370
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:01,177
about Ford settling out of court.

371
00:13:01,237 --> 00:13:03,236
Cases settled out of court or by judgement

372
00:13:03,237 --> 00:13:05,477
against Ford or its co-defendants:

373
00:13:05,537 --> 00:13:06,337
eight.

374
00:13:06,367 --> 00:13:07,346
Cases pending trial:

375
00:13:07,347 --> 00:13:08,557
nineteen.

376
00:13:08,617 --> 00:13:10,416
Cases settled in favour of Ford

377
00:13:10,417 --> 00:13:11,897
or under investigation:

378
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:12,897
two.

379
00:13:12,957 --> 00:13:15,616
Then the agency added everything it had from every

380
00:13:15,617 --> 00:13:18,120
source, and wrote one paragraph.

381
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:20,419
It is the paragraph this whole film exists

382
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:22,553
to put back into circulation.

383
00:13:22,613 --> 00:13:24,733
In total, the agency wrote,

384
00:13:24,793 --> 00:13:27,052
the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration

385
00:13:27,053 --> 00:13:28,172
is aware of thirty-

386
00:13:28,173 --> 00:13:30,492
eight cases in which rear-end collisions

387
00:13:30,493 --> 00:13:32,452
of Pinto vehicles have resulted

388
00:13:32,453 --> 00:13:34,093
in fuel tank damage,

389
00:13:34,153 --> 00:13:37,249
fuel system leakage and-or ensuing fire.

390
00:13:37,309 --> 00:13:39,208
These cases have resulted in a total

391
00:13:39,209 --> 00:13:41,108
of twenty-seven fatalities sustained

392
00:13:41,109 --> 00:13:42,529
by Pinto occupants,

393
00:13:42,589 --> 00:13:45,168
of which one is reported to have resulted

394
00:13:45,169 --> 00:13:46,837
from impact injuries.

395
00:13:46,897 --> 00:13:48,716
In addition, twenty-four occupants

396
00:13:48,717 --> 00:13:51,316
of these Pinto vehicles have sustained non-fatal

397
00:13:51,317 --> 00:13:52,617
burn injuries.

398
00:13:52,677 --> 00:13:54,124
Twenty-seven.

399
00:13:54,184 --> 00:13:57,443
One of them from the impact rather than the fire.

400
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,822
And because this film is about people quoting

401
00:13:59,823 --> 00:14:02,042
a number without its document,

402
00:14:02,043 --> 00:14:03,653
here is the rest of the document.

403
00:14:03,654 --> 00:14:06,074
The agency set out, in its own words,

404
00:14:06,134 --> 00:14:08,910
why its data might be wrong in both directions.

405
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:11,449
Fire or explosion is not a standard data element

406
00:14:11,450 --> 00:14:13,715
on most police reporting forms.

407
00:14:13,775 --> 00:14:15,954
If a death due to burns occurred sometime

408
00:14:15,955 --> 00:14:17,455
after the crash,

409
00:14:17,515 --> 00:14:19,434
it is less likely that it would be reported

410
00:14:19,435 --> 00:14:21,770
on the officer's accident report.

411
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:24,449
The system does not record the cause of death,

412
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:25,790
only its fact;

413
00:14:25,850 --> 00:14:27,829
it does not distinguish between deaths due

414
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:30,522
to impact and those caused by the fire.

415
00:14:30,582 --> 00:14:32,122
That is the number.

416
00:14:32,182 --> 00:14:32,781
Twenty-seven,

417
00:14:32,782 --> 00:14:35,181
with the government's own reasons for doubting it,

418
00:14:35,182 --> 00:14:36,462
attached.

419
00:14:36,522 --> 00:14:39,141
In May nineteen seventy-eight the agency issued

420
00:14:39,142 --> 00:14:40,801
an initial determination

421
00:14:40,802 --> 00:14:43,081
that the Pinto's fuel system was defective,

422
00:14:43,082 --> 00:14:45,861
and scheduled a hearing for the fourteenth of June

423
00:14:45,862 --> 00:14:46,991
to enable Ford to reply.

424
00:14:46,992 --> 00:14:48,857
The hearing never happened.

425
00:14:48,917 --> 00:14:51,456
On the nineteenth of June the agency received

426
00:14:51,457 --> 00:14:52,547
a recall.

427
00:14:52,607 --> 00:14:55,726
Campaign seven eight V one four three.

428
00:14:55,786 --> 00:14:58,487
One million four hundred thousand vehicles.

429
00:14:58,547 --> 00:15:00,646
The remedy was a longer fuel filler pipe

430
00:15:00,647 --> 00:15:01,886
with an improved seal,

431
00:15:01,887 --> 00:15:04,886
and a polyethylene shield installed on the front

432
00:15:04,887 --> 00:15:06,171
of the fuel tank.

433
00:15:06,231 --> 00:15:07,450
Twelve days after a jury

434
00:15:07,451 --> 00:15:09,629
in California returned its verdict.

435
00:15:09,689 --> 00:15:12,344
Five days before the agency's hearing.

436
00:15:12,404 --> 00:15:14,283
And one last figure for this act,

437
00:15:14,284 --> 00:15:17,056
which is the least famous number in the story.

438
00:15:17,116 --> 00:15:19,036
According to an agency official,

439
00:15:19,096 --> 00:15:20,695
only fifty-three per cent

440
00:15:20,696 --> 00:15:22,215
of Pinto owners responded

441
00:15:22,216 --> 00:15:24,435
to the recall offer extended by Ford

442
00:15:24,436 --> 00:15:25,994
in nineteen seventy-eight.

443
00:15:26,054 --> 00:15:30,554
Just over half the cars came back.

444
00:15:30,783 --> 00:15:33,082
Nobody, in fifty years of telling this story,

445
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:35,621
has read out the title of the table.

446
00:15:35,681 --> 00:15:36,571
So.

447
00:15:36,631 --> 00:15:37,890
The document has a name,

448
00:15:37,891 --> 00:15:40,726
and it is not the one it is usually given.

449
00:15:40,786 --> 00:15:43,005
It is called Fatalities Associated

450
00:15:43,006 --> 00:15:45,365
with Crash Induced Fuel Leakage and Fires,

451
00:15:45,366 --> 00:15:48,445
by E. S. Grush and C. S. Saunby,

452
00:15:48,446 --> 00:15:50,525
on the letterhead of Ford's Environmental

453
00:15:50,526 --> 00:15:52,466
and Safety Engineering office,

454
00:15:52,526 --> 00:15:54,586
and it is headed Attachment Two.

455
00:15:54,646 --> 00:15:56,186
Attachment to what?

456
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:57,625
To a submission Ford filed

457
00:15:57,626 --> 00:15:59,845
with the federal regulator on the nineteenth

458
00:15:59,846 --> 00:16:03,085
of September, nineteen seventy-three,

459
00:16:03,086 --> 00:16:05,405
captioned a Petition for Reconsideration

460
00:16:05,406 --> 00:16:08,171
of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard Number

461
00:16:08,207 --> 00:16:08,991
Three Oh One.

462
00:16:08,992 --> 00:16:11,415
It is not an internal memorandum.

463
00:16:11,475 --> 00:16:12,830
It is a filing.

464
00:16:12,890 --> 00:16:15,070
It says so in its first paragraph:

465
00:16:15,130 --> 00:16:16,869
the agency has issued Notice Two

466
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:19,929
of Docket seventy dash twenty, and Notice One

467
00:16:19,930 --> 00:16:22,529
of Docket seventy-three dash twenty,

468
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:24,288
both regarding fuel system integrity.

469
00:16:24,289 --> 00:16:27,687
And on page four it says what it is analysing.

470
00:16:27,747 --> 00:16:29,646
The analysis discussed below concerns

471
00:16:29,647 --> 00:16:31,606
the static rollover requirement proposed

472
00:16:31,607 --> 00:16:34,063
for the standard.

473
00:16:34,123 --> 00:16:35,718
Rollover.

474
00:16:35,778 --> 00:16:37,597
Not rear impact.

475
00:16:37,657 --> 00:16:39,290
A car turning over.

476
00:16:39,350 --> 00:16:40,829
The paper contradicts itself

477
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:42,969
on which standard number that requirement belongs

478
00:16:42,970 --> 00:16:44,110
to —

479
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:46,569
page four says three oh one

480
00:16:46,570 --> 00:16:50,349
and the table caption says two oh eight —

481
00:16:50,350 --> 00:16:52,409
and rather than quietly pick one,

482
00:16:52,410 --> 00:16:53,999
this film tells you the paper does that.

483
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,739
Schwartz, who went and found the filing,

484
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:57,380
states it in one sentence:

485
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,039
it was the rollover situation,

486
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:01,779
and not the rear-end-impact situation,

487
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:04,735
that was the subject of the Ford document.

488
00:17:04,795 --> 00:17:07,636
Now the table itself, one line at a time.

489
00:17:07,696 --> 00:17:08,295
Savings:

490
00:17:08,296 --> 00:17:12,676
one hundred and eighty burn deaths,

491
00:17:12,736 --> 00:17:14,479
one hundred and eighty serious burn injuries,

492
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:15,054
two thousand one hundred burned vehicles.

493
00:17:15,055 --> 00:17:16,295
Unit cost:

494
00:17:16,355 --> 00:17:21,650
two hundred thousand dollars per death,
sixty-seven thousand per injury,

495
00:17:21,651 --> 00:17:22,181
seven hundred per vehicle.

496
00:17:22,182 --> 00:17:23,162
Total benefit,

497
00:17:23,222 --> 00:17:25,267
forty-nine and a half million dollars.

498
00:17:25,268 --> 00:17:26,487
And then the line that makes it

499
00:17:26,488 --> 00:17:27,527
a different document

500
00:17:27,528 --> 00:17:30,524
from the one everybody thinks they are quoting.

501
00:17:30,584 --> 00:17:30,943
Sales:

502
00:17:30,944 --> 00:17:32,682
eleven million cars.

503
00:17:32,742 --> 00:17:35,165
One and a half million light trucks.

504
00:17:35,225 --> 00:17:37,926
Eleven million cars is not a Ford model line.

505
00:17:37,986 --> 00:17:40,455
It is the American market for a year.

506
00:17:40,515 --> 00:17:42,520
The paper says so itself.

507
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:44,059
The retail price equivalent

508
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:46,259
of the vehicle modifications necessary

509
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,379
to assure compliance

510
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,299
with the static rollover portion

511
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:51,679
of the proposed standard has been determined

512
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:52,939
by Ford to be an average

513
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:55,459
of eleven dollars per passenger car

514
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:57,588
and eleven dollars per light truck.

515
00:17:57,648 --> 00:17:59,167
While these are Ford costs,

516
00:17:59,168 --> 00:18:02,160
they have been applied across the industry
in this analysis.

517
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,921
The word Pinto does not appear in that table.

518
00:18:04,981 --> 00:18:07,000
Two more things the same eight pages say,

519
00:18:07,001 --> 00:18:09,911
and they cut in opposite directions.

520
00:18:09,971 --> 00:18:12,487
The first is Ford arguing its own case.

521
00:18:12,547 --> 00:18:14,706
The agency's estimate of fatalities

522
00:18:14,707 --> 00:18:17,867
in fire-involved crashes, the report says,

523
00:18:17,927 --> 00:18:19,646
appears to overstate the seriousness

524
00:18:19,647 --> 00:18:21,239
of the fire problem.

525
00:18:21,299 --> 00:18:23,858
The basis is a sample of twenty-four, of whom,

526
00:18:23,859 --> 00:18:26,678
the paper says, in over half of the instances

527
00:18:26,679 --> 00:18:28,969
the deceased was not burned at all.

528
00:18:29,029 --> 00:18:30,869
The second is the opposite,

529
00:18:30,929 --> 00:18:33,867
and it is the strangest fact in this episode.

530
00:18:33,927 --> 00:18:36,106
On page one, the same report tells the government

531
00:18:36,107 --> 00:18:38,486
that the likelihood of a given crash resulting

532
00:18:38,487 --> 00:18:42,227
in fuel spillage is much higher for rear impacts —

533
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,766
twenty-six per cent with spillage

534
00:18:43,767 --> 00:18:45,426
in the sample studied —

535
00:18:45,427 --> 00:18:48,106
than for other crash types, such as frontals,

536
00:18:48,107 --> 00:18:49,783
at three and a half per cent.

537
00:18:49,784 --> 00:18:51,003
The document that is quoted

538
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:53,163
to prove Ford ignored rear-impact fires

539
00:18:53,164 --> 00:18:54,423
is a document that told

540
00:18:54,424 --> 00:18:56,663
the federal government rear impact was by far

541
00:18:56,664 --> 00:18:58,105
the worst case.

542
00:18:58,165 --> 00:19:00,832
Which leaves the two hundred thousand dollars.

543
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:02,532
The report attributes it, twice,

544
00:19:02,533 --> 00:19:03,859
to the government.

545
00:19:03,919 --> 00:19:05,778
The agency has calculated a value

546
00:19:05,779 --> 00:19:08,676
of two hundred thousand dollars for each fatality.

547
00:19:08,677 --> 00:19:10,542
And it goes further than that.

548
00:19:10,602 --> 00:19:13,201
The casualty to dollars conversion factors used

549
00:19:13,202 --> 00:19:14,962
in this study, it says,

550
00:19:15,022 --> 00:19:17,061
were the societal cost values prepared

551
00:19:17,062 --> 00:19:18,458
by the agency.

552
00:19:18,518 --> 00:19:19,897
These values are generally higher

553
00:19:19,898 --> 00:19:22,722
than similarly-defined costs from other sources,

554
00:19:22,778 --> 00:19:25,677
and their use does not signify that Ford accepts

555
00:19:25,678 --> 00:19:27,721
or concurs in the values.

556
00:19:27,781 --> 00:19:30,111
And a shorter film would stop there.

557
00:19:30,171 --> 00:19:31,430
The man who established most

558
00:19:31,431 --> 00:19:34,019
of that changed his mind about it, in print.

559
00:19:34,047 --> 00:19:36,126
Schwartz first concluded that Ford's use

560
00:19:36,127 --> 00:19:37,746
of the figure was clearly proper,

561
00:19:37,747 --> 00:19:39,746
because it was the same datum

562
00:19:39,747 --> 00:19:41,625
the regulator would be using.

563
00:19:41,685 --> 00:19:44,260
Then, in his words, he did further homework.

564
00:19:44,261 --> 00:19:47,000
Contrary to my earlier understanding, he wrote,

565
00:19:47,001 --> 00:19:49,480
in its standard-setting the agency was not,

566
00:19:49,481 --> 00:19:51,740
in the early nineteen seventies, relying

567
00:19:51,741 --> 00:19:54,191
on a two hundred thousand dollar life-value

568
00:19:54,192 --> 00:19:54,637
figure.

569
00:19:54,638 --> 00:19:57,678
It was taking costs and benefits into account,

570
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,457
and essentially finessing the question

571
00:19:59,458 --> 00:20:01,338
of the monetary value of life,

572
00:20:01,398 --> 00:20:03,617
while at the same time releasing documents

573
00:20:03,618 --> 00:20:04,417
that set forth

574
00:20:04,418 --> 00:20:07,974
a two hundred thousand dollar life-value datum.

575
00:20:08,034 --> 00:20:10,550
There is more, and it is worse for Ford.

576
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:13,129
The government's nineteen seventy-two report

577
00:20:13,130 --> 00:20:16,650
had said that its own figure represented

578
00:20:16,710 --> 00:20:18,929
the minimum, but not the maximum,

579
00:20:18,930 --> 00:20:20,452
that society should spend

580
00:20:20,512 --> 00:20:23,260
in preventing highway fatalities.
Schwartz's conclusion on that:

581
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:26,119
the nineteen seventy-three Ford report can fairly

582
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:29,020
be faulted for not taking account

583
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:31,309
of the agency's explanation of the implications

584
00:20:31,310 --> 00:20:33,948
of its own figure.
Ford's answer, also in the record,

585
00:20:33,949 --> 00:20:36,228
is that it used the government's number in part

586
00:20:36,229 --> 00:20:38,968
because it was higher
than other life-value estimates known

587
00:20:38,969 --> 00:20:40,243
to the company.

588
00:20:40,303 --> 00:20:42,182
So the honest version is narrower

589
00:20:42,183 --> 00:20:44,119
than the popular correction.

590
00:20:44,179 --> 00:20:45,938
The two hundred thousand dollars

591
00:20:45,939 --> 00:20:47,775
is the government's published figure.

592
00:20:47,776 --> 00:20:50,247
It was not the government's decision rule.

593
00:20:50,259 --> 00:20:51,878
And Ford can fairly be faulted

594
00:20:51,879 --> 00:20:53,618
for using it without saying what

595
00:20:53,619 --> 00:20:55,295
the government said about it.

596
00:20:55,296 --> 00:20:56,178
One more thing,

597
00:20:56,236 --> 00:20:58,787
and it is small and it is not small.

598
00:20:58,847 --> 00:21:00,387
Mother Jones knew.

599
00:21:00,447 --> 00:21:03,586
In a nineteen seventy-two report, Dowie wrote,

600
00:21:03,587 --> 00:21:04,646
the agency decided

601
00:21:04,647 --> 00:21:08,116
a human life was worth two hundred thousand seven

602
00:21:08,117 --> 00:21:11,386
hundred and twenty-five dollars.
That sentence is two sentences after the line

603
00:21:11,387 --> 00:21:13,944
about Ford having a better idea.

604
00:21:14,004 --> 00:21:15,603
The correction was already in the article

605
00:21:15,604 --> 00:21:17,263
that created the problem.

606
00:21:17,323 --> 00:21:19,699
And that report was never in evidence.

607
00:21:19,759 --> 00:21:21,758
The appellate opinion records Ford's objection

608
00:21:21,759 --> 00:21:25,139
to counsel's closing argument in these terms:

609
00:21:25,199 --> 00:21:27,598
Ford argues that the documentation referred

610
00:21:27,599 --> 00:21:30,819
to by Mr Copp, the Grush-Saunby Report,

611
00:21:30,879 --> 00:21:32,816
was excluded from evidence.

612
00:21:32,876 --> 00:21:35,475
The jury that returned one hundred

613
00:21:35,476 --> 00:21:37,262
and twenty-five million dollars never saw it.

614
00:21:37,263 --> 00:21:39,639
Schwartz gives the procedural history.

615
00:21:39,699 --> 00:21:41,378
The plaintiffs did not even claim

616
00:21:41,379 --> 00:21:43,618
that the document was relevant to the issue

617
00:21:43,619 --> 00:21:44,939
of liability;

618
00:21:44,999 --> 00:21:46,858
they attempted to introduce it on the issue

619
00:21:46,859 --> 00:21:48,279
of punitive damages,

620
00:21:48,339 --> 00:21:51,224
as indicative of Ford's corporate mentality.

621
00:21:51,284 --> 00:21:53,303
After considering the matter over a period

622
00:21:53,304 --> 00:21:54,704
of several weeks,

623
00:21:54,764 --> 00:21:57,352
the trial judge ruled against admissibility.

624
00:21:57,389 --> 00:21:59,468
And in a footnote he gives the judge's reason,

625
00:21:59,469 --> 00:22:02,691
which is the last thing anyone would guess.

626
00:22:02,751 --> 00:22:05,050
A primary reason given by the trial judge

627
00:22:05,051 --> 00:22:06,750
in ruling against the admissibility

628
00:22:06,751 --> 00:22:09,310
of the Ford report was that Ford was using

629
00:22:09,311 --> 00:22:12,233
the figure that the agency itself preferred.

630
00:22:12,293 --> 00:22:14,412
The document was kept out because the number

631
00:22:14,413 --> 00:22:16,261
in it belonged to the government.

632
00:22:16,262 --> 00:22:17,152
So.

633
00:22:17,212 --> 00:22:18,474
Two prices.

634
00:22:18,534 --> 00:22:20,973
Eleven dollars is a rollover-compliance figure,

635
00:22:20,974 --> 00:22:23,853
for every passenger car and light truck sold

636
00:22:23,854 --> 00:22:27,293
in America, in a nineteen seventy-three filing

637
00:22:27,294 --> 00:22:28,759
that a court excluded.

638
00:22:28,819 --> 00:22:30,158
Fifteen dollars

639
00:22:30,159 --> 00:22:33,158
and thirty cents is an appellate court's figure

640
00:22:33,159 --> 00:22:35,298
for a package of rear-impact fixes

641
00:22:35,299 --> 00:22:38,626
on one car line, in an opinion that stands.

642
00:22:38,686 --> 00:22:40,691
They are not the same number.

643
00:22:40,751 --> 00:22:43,559
They never were.

644
00:22:43,619 --> 00:22:46,078
On the tenth of August, nineteen seventy-eight,

645
00:22:46,079 --> 00:22:47,958
in Elkhart County, Indiana,

646
00:22:47,959 --> 00:22:49,818
three young women died after a van struck

647
00:22:49,819 --> 00:22:51,382
the Pinto they were in.

648
00:22:51,442 --> 00:22:52,621
The wire report named them:

649
00:22:52,622 --> 00:22:55,722
Judy Ulrich, eighteen, of Osceola, Indiana;

650
00:22:55,782 --> 00:22:57,723
her sixteen-year-old sister Lynn;

651
00:22:57,742 --> 00:22:59,921
and their cousin Donna Ulrich, eighteen,

652
00:22:59,922 --> 00:23:01,667
of Roanoke, Illinois.

653
00:23:01,727 --> 00:23:04,243
A grand jury indicted the company.

654
00:23:04,303 --> 00:23:06,082
Three counts of reckless homicide,

655
00:23:06,083 --> 00:23:08,630
and one count of criminal recklessness.

656
00:23:08,690 --> 00:23:10,709
The maximum penalties would total thirty-six

657
00:23:10,710 --> 00:23:12,599
thousand dollars in fines.

658
00:23:12,659 --> 00:23:14,246
Thirty-six thousand.

659
00:23:14,306 --> 00:23:16,005
Against a company whose net worth

660
00:23:16,006 --> 00:23:18,165
the California trial judge had put

661
00:23:18,166 --> 00:23:20,351
at seven point seven billion.

662
00:23:20,411 --> 00:23:22,830
The grand jury could have indicted individual Ford

663
00:23:22,831 --> 00:23:24,041
executives.

664
00:23:24,101 --> 00:23:26,988
It chose to charge only the corporation.

665
00:23:27,048 --> 00:23:28,648
This case has two numbers,

666
00:23:28,708 --> 00:23:30,737
and that is a fact about its shape.

667
00:23:30,738 --> 00:23:32,397
It was filed in Elkhart Superior Court

668
00:23:32,398 --> 00:23:38,217
as number five three two four, on the thirteenth

669
00:23:38,218 --> 00:23:40,537
of September nineteen seventy-eight —
and the source

670
00:23:40,538 --> 00:23:44,717
for that is a California appellate opinion five

671
00:23:44,718 --> 00:23:45,428
years later,

672
00:23:45,429 --> 00:23:45,682
surveying every corporate homicide prosecution

673
00:23:45,683 --> 00:23:47,284
then known.
The venue then changed,

674
00:23:47,285 --> 00:23:49,084
and judgment was entered at Winamac,

675
00:23:49,085 --> 00:23:51,344
in the Pulaski County Circuit Court,

676
00:23:51,345 --> 00:23:54,406
as number eleven dash four three one.

677
00:23:54,466 --> 00:23:56,378
The trial ran ten weeks.

678
00:23:56,438 --> 00:23:58,437
And here is the structural fact that explains

679
00:23:58,438 --> 00:24:01,177
the whole thing, which almost nobody who tells

680
00:24:01,178 --> 00:24:03,319
this story has ever mentioned.

681
00:24:03,379 --> 00:24:05,938
The reckless homicide statute Indiana charged

682
00:24:05,939 --> 00:24:07,698
under had been enacted only

683
00:24:07,699 --> 00:24:09,470
in nineteen seventy-seven.

684
00:24:09,530 --> 00:24:11,609
So Ford could not be prosecuted

685
00:24:11,610 --> 00:24:14,321
for the reckless design of the Pinto.

686
00:24:14,381 --> 00:24:16,820
The prosecution needed to show a reckless failure,

687
00:24:16,821 --> 00:24:19,741
after nineteen seventy-seven,

688
00:24:19,801 --> 00:24:20,857
to repair or to warn.

689
00:24:20,858 --> 00:24:22,909
The design was not on trial.

690
00:24:22,969 --> 00:24:24,416
It could not be.

691
00:24:24,476 --> 00:24:26,515
And largely because of the narrowness

692
00:24:26,516 --> 00:24:28,536
of the resulting issue,

693
00:24:28,596 --> 00:24:30,655
the prosecution was not able to secure

694
00:24:30,656 --> 00:24:32,795
the admission of the internal Ford documents

695
00:24:32,796 --> 00:24:35,722
on which it had hoped to build its case.

696
00:24:35,782 --> 00:24:38,251
What was left was a fight about speed.

697
00:24:38,311 --> 00:24:40,230
The defence showed films of test crashes

698
00:24:40,231 --> 00:24:42,430
in which other cars struck by the same model

699
00:24:42,431 --> 00:24:45,238
of van sustained similar damage.

700
00:24:45,298 --> 00:24:47,798
The prosecutor described the resources:

701
00:24:47,858 --> 00:24:50,623
it has just been a matter of David and Goliath.

702
00:24:50,660 --> 00:24:53,219
On the thirteenth of March nineteen eighty,

703
00:24:53,220 --> 00:24:55,358
the jury found Ford not guilty.

704
00:24:55,418 --> 00:24:57,657
The Indiana Law Review, surveying the year,

705
00:24:57,658 --> 00:24:59,943
recorded what the jurors said afterwards.

706
00:24:59,944 --> 00:25:02,343
Interviews with the jury after trial indicated

707
00:25:02,344 --> 00:25:04,943
that the issue of closing speed was never resolved

708
00:25:04,944 --> 00:25:06,175
by the jury.

709
00:25:06,235 --> 00:25:09,122
The case was not appealed from the trial level.

710
00:25:09,182 --> 00:25:11,481
That is why there is no Indiana appellate opinion

711
00:25:11,482 --> 00:25:13,002
about any of this,

712
00:25:13,062 --> 00:25:15,501
and why almost everything written about that trial

713
00:25:15,502 --> 00:25:19,221
since has come from two newspapers and a book.

714
00:25:19,281 --> 00:25:22,168
So the popular story is wrong in five places.

715
00:25:22,228 --> 00:25:24,418
The document is about rollover.

716
00:25:24,478 --> 00:25:26,994
The units are the whole industry.

717
00:25:27,054 --> 00:25:29,721
The price of a life belonged to the government.

718
00:25:29,722 --> 00:25:31,634
The jury never saw the paper.

719
00:25:31,694 --> 00:25:34,442
And the criminal case ended in an acquittal.

720
00:25:34,502 --> 00:25:36,421
None of which makes the car innocent,

721
00:25:36,422 --> 00:25:38,321
and the man who established most of it says

722
00:25:38,322 --> 00:25:40,268
so on the same pages.

723
00:25:40,328 --> 00:25:42,368
In the government's crash-testing,

724
00:25:42,428 --> 00:25:43,588
Schwartz writes,

725
00:25:43,648 --> 00:25:46,368
the Pinto was compared to the Chevrolet Vega,

726
00:25:46,428 --> 00:25:49,087
often regarded as having the least safe gas tank

727
00:25:49,088 --> 00:25:52,224
of the other subcompacts for sale in America.

728
00:25:52,284 --> 00:25:53,264
In this process,

729
00:25:53,324 --> 00:25:54,863
the Pinto consistently flunked tests

730
00:25:54,864 --> 00:25:56,889
that the Vega was able to pass.

731
00:25:56,949 --> 00:25:58,228
At the criminal trial,

732
00:25:58,229 --> 00:25:59,688
Ford put in exhibits showing

733
00:25:59,689 --> 00:26:01,968
that Pintos were one point nine per cent

734
00:26:01,969 --> 00:26:04,768
of the cars on American roads and were involved

735
00:26:04,769 --> 00:26:07,168
in one point nine per cent

736
00:26:07,169 --> 00:26:10,866
of fatal accidents accompanied by fire.
The prosecution's own expert confirmed Ford's

737
00:26:10,867 --> 00:26:11,746
data.

738
00:26:11,806 --> 00:26:14,005
Then the same expert narrowed it to the accidents

739
00:26:14,006 --> 00:26:16,546
that were actually the subject of the case:

740
00:26:16,606 --> 00:26:19,105
rear-end fire fatalities.

741
00:26:19,165 --> 00:26:20,824
These data showed that Pintos,

742
00:26:20,825 --> 00:26:22,824
while comprising one point nine per cent

743
00:26:22,825 --> 00:26:24,984
of the auto population,

744
00:26:24,985 --> 00:26:27,583
were responsible for four point one per cent

745
00:26:27,643 --> 00:26:30,247
of all such fatalities.
One point nine of the cars.

746
00:26:30,307 --> 00:26:32,312
Four point one of the deaths.

747
00:26:32,372 --> 00:26:33,171
And then the fact

748
00:26:33,172 --> 00:26:35,770
this film has been walking towards.

749
00:26:35,830 --> 00:26:38,392
Ford had its own comparative memorandum.

750
00:26:38,452 --> 00:26:38,851
It showed

751
00:26:38,852 --> 00:26:41,491
the Pinto's rear-fire fatality rate below

752
00:26:41,492 --> 00:26:42,091
the Gremlin's,

753
00:26:42,092 --> 00:26:44,871
and considerably above the respective rates

754
00:26:44,872 --> 00:26:48,212
of the Vega, Toyota, Mazda and Datsun.

755
00:26:48,272 --> 00:26:49,852
Schwartz's next clause:

756
00:26:49,912 --> 00:26:51,131
perhaps for this reason,

757
00:26:51,132 --> 00:26:53,571
Ford did not introduce the memorandum during

758
00:26:53,572 --> 00:26:55,014
the criminal trial.

759
00:26:55,074 --> 00:26:57,113
The company that was acquitted had a document

760
00:26:57,114 --> 00:26:58,093
that would have hurt it,

761
00:26:58,094 --> 00:26:59,819
and did not put it in.

762
00:26:59,879 --> 00:27:01,198
And the professor who took

763
00:27:01,199 --> 00:27:03,370
the myth apart ends up here.

764
00:27:03,430 --> 00:27:05,630
There was a package of changes —

765
00:27:05,690 --> 00:27:07,110
a stronger bumper,

766
00:27:07,170 --> 00:27:09,210
a smooth bolt-free differential,

767
00:27:09,270 --> 00:27:11,230
hat sections and cross-members —

768
00:27:11,290 --> 00:27:13,887
that would have improved the Pinto's safety.

769
00:27:13,947 --> 00:27:15,786
According to the evidence, he writes,

770
00:27:15,787 --> 00:27:16,826
the overall cost

771
00:27:16,827 --> 00:27:19,946
of this combination would have been nine dollars.

772
00:27:20,006 --> 00:27:22,226
It makes sense to assume, he goes on,

773
00:27:22,286 --> 00:27:24,185
that these items were turned down primarily

774
00:27:24,186 --> 00:27:26,469
on account of their monetary costs.

775
00:27:26,529 --> 00:27:27,948
It is plausible to believe

776
00:27:27,949 --> 00:27:30,009
that because of these costs,

777
00:27:30,069 --> 00:27:32,909
Ford decided not to improve the Pinto's design,

778
00:27:32,969 --> 00:27:34,748
knowing that its decision would increase

779
00:27:34,749 --> 00:27:37,822
the chances of the loss of consumer life.

780
00:27:37,882 --> 00:27:38,601
Once a variety

781
00:27:38,602 --> 00:27:40,962
of misconceptions are stripped away,

782
00:27:41,022 --> 00:27:45,566
this limited core of the Pinto story remains.

783
00:27:45,626 --> 00:27:47,213
Thirty-eight cases.

784
00:27:47,273 --> 00:27:50,439
Twenty-seven deaths, one of them from the impact.

785
00:27:50,499 --> 00:27:53,665
Twenty-four burn injuries that were not fatal.

786
00:27:53,725 --> 00:27:55,584
That is the government's own count,

787
00:27:55,585 --> 00:27:57,744
from May nineteen seventy-eight,

788
00:27:57,745 --> 00:28:00,293
with the government's own doubts attached to it.

789
00:28:00,294 --> 00:28:02,613
The rest of what this film stands on ends

790
00:28:02,614 --> 00:28:05,793
on the tenth of September, nineteen eighty-one,

791
00:28:05,794 --> 00:28:08,173
when the California Supreme Court declined to hear

792
00:28:08,174 --> 00:28:09,172
the case.

793
00:28:09,232 --> 00:28:10,352
As for Winamac,

794
00:28:10,412 --> 00:28:12,251
a court in another state wrote down the number,

795
00:28:12,252 --> 00:28:15,649
and a law review in Indiana wrote down the date.

796
00:28:15,709 --> 00:28:17,868
The indictment itself is still in a ledger

797
00:28:17,869 --> 00:28:21,290
in Elkhart County, and this film did not get it.

798
00:28:21,350 --> 00:28:22,749
Eleven dollars,

799
00:28:22,750 --> 00:28:24,575
and fifteen dollars and thirty cents.

800
00:28:24,576 --> 00:28:26,755
Schwartz again, and this is the sentence

801
00:28:26,756 --> 00:28:29,553
the last fifty years should have been built on.

802
00:28:29,613 --> 00:28:31,832
Even if the general portrayal of the Pinto

803
00:28:31,833 --> 00:28:35,293
as a firetrap should be rejected as false,

804
00:28:35,353 --> 00:28:38,373
a limited core of that myth seems fair enough:

805
00:28:38,433 --> 00:28:39,372
the Pinto's record

806
00:28:39,373 --> 00:28:41,672
in rear-end fire fatalities was not only much

807
00:28:41,673 --> 00:28:43,733
worse than the all-car average,

808
00:28:43,793 --> 00:28:46,032
but was apparently somewhat worse than the record

809
00:28:46,033 --> 00:28:47,693
of most, though not all,

810
00:28:47,753 --> 00:28:50,008
of its subcompact competitors.

811
00:28:50,068 --> 00:28:51,933
And his last word on the car.

812
00:28:51,993 --> 00:28:53,612
From what I have been able to learn,

813
00:28:53,613 --> 00:28:55,632
as for safety the Pinto was a car

814
00:28:55,633 --> 00:28:58,317
that was neither admirable nor despicable.

815
00:28:58,377 --> 00:29:00,676
Its overall fatality rate was roughly

816
00:29:00,677 --> 00:29:03,215
in the middle of the subcompact range.

817
00:29:03,275 --> 00:29:05,734
Its record was better than the subcompact average

818
00:29:05,735 --> 00:29:08,345
with respect to fatalities with fire.

819
00:29:08,405 --> 00:29:10,984
Yet for the quite small category of fatalities

820
00:29:10,985 --> 00:29:12,785
with rear-end fire,

821
00:29:12,845 --> 00:29:14,724
its design features apparently gave it

822
00:29:14,725 --> 00:29:16,540
a worse-than-average record.

823
00:29:16,600 --> 00:29:17,019
Hence,

824
00:29:17,020 --> 00:29:19,239
there was nothing clearly wrong in subjecting Ford

825
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:20,819
